{
  "reasons": {
    "added-2-36": "Either Brenton adds it to make English of a Greek phrase ('away' of 'cast away', 'back', 'forth', 'aside', 'own', 'very', 'highly', 'round', 'because', 'cause', 'means', 'together', 'ever', 'thing') or the Greek word that renders it is a pair the aligner made to another English word, which the model pass does not move ('scorn' of 'laugh them to scorn', 'pieces' of 'dash them in pieces', 'afflict', 'chasten', 'enrich', 'tends', 'cheers', 'week' of 'the first day of the week', 'overlook', 'compassion', 'honored', 'fret' of 'fret not yourself'), each read against its verse (mw-u2w5klk.349.13).",
    "other-verse-2-36": "LXX2012's English here renders Greek of the verse before or after, or Greek that Swete's verse does not have, so a chunk cannot point at it (the like of Genesis 37:32): the last clause of Psalm 16:3 is the Greek of 16:4's first words, 16:8's 'from those that resist your right hand' is the end of the Greek 16:7, 33:17's 'The righteous cried, and the Lord listened to them' and the 'delivered' of 33:18 are the Greek of 33:18, 33:20's 'Lord will deliver' the Greek 33:21's Κύριος, and 15:2's 'have no need of my goodness' has no Greek in the verse as Swete has it (mw-u2w5klk.349.13)."
  },
